\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shuffled onto Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s white wood, elevated veranda. The space was enclosed by a diamond trellis, thick with vines. No slipshod carpentry here, no nails, nothing but clean joinery and a mastery of craft that was impossible to appreciate unless one has personally experienced the difficulty of hiding an edge.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The expense of this veranda was not justified. It should have overlooked a vineyard, or at the very least, a brown brick patio full of laughter as naked youths bathed in a tiered fountain. Instead, when Mandri peeked through the diamond gaps in the trellis, he was greeted with the horror of Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s estate: twelve, massive, man-made leech lakes. The waters were each a different shade of dark green. Under the surface, the leeches were so numerous that they looked like rippling clouds.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Each lake was a perfect square. The edges of the nearest lakes were lined with roofless stalls, with each stall penning a live animal into the shallows. Goats, horses, cows; any animal larger than a large dog would do. They were each slumped onto support beams. Their snouts were tied into bags of intoxicating freeweed smoke. This was not an act of beneficence to inure them to the pain, it was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s way of keeping his peaceful country air free of their wild moaning.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The rest of the estate was mostly flies and marshgrass. The sky was cloudy with the kind of tall, mountainous clouds that swallowed landscape paintings whole, the kind that cast broad shadows down upon the world to pull the viewer through the distance, as they pulled Mandri now, all the way out to the sparkling blue line on the horizon which was the sea.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram set himself to work in setting up an easel which he claimed to have built himself. Slaves cut and planed the lumber, brewed the glue, hammered the metal fittings, but Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s mighty mind designed it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you sure you want to do this here?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked as he paced about.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not here?\u8221\'94 said Vigram.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri eyed the distressed animals in the lakes below. Shaved down to the pink skin like criminals, they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been reduced to bags of blood. Leechmen waded between the stalls so that they could trowel off the largest leeches and toss them into grass baskets. Those leeches which weren\u8217\'92t engaged in the constant struggle for the cleanest spot of flesh were mating. If only those foul creatures understood how their orgy was a prelude to death.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s stomach turned. He\u8217\'92d eaten more than his fill of Meskalimi leech. All those goats, horses, and cows were suffering in leech paradise on account of him. Who was he to judge Vigram\u8217\'92s trade? What right did he have to feel disgusted with this place?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he eyed the patio\u8217\'92s trellis. \u8220\'93These vines aren\u8217\'92t yet thick enough for a solid shadow. A dappled light will fall upon the sitter. It\u8217\'92s going to make things difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He moved through the dappled light to demonstrate the effect on his own skin.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My dear Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, his drawl rolling heavily. \u8220\'93The patterns of light and shadow are a magical vesture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 Mandri pondered, \u8220\'93I might suggest that you worry about \u8216\'91magical vestures\u8217\'92 when you\u8217\'92re skilled enough to make a face look like\u8230\'85a face.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said firmly, long beard wiggling. \u8220\'93I won\u8217\'92t have it any other way. A magical vesture for a magical subject.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As if bidden from the ether by Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s words, a woman draped in a long russet robe stepped out of the dark interior of the house. Younger than Vigram, older than Mandri, this Jandri beauty was tall, thin, with clear brown skin, sun-kissed cheeks, and long black hair which swept around her neck, then fell over her shoulder. Her fierce green eyes lent her stern expression a watchful aspect. As she neared, it became clear that she was a predator.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri supposed that she was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s slave. Her robe was very simple and spun from a host of earthy threads, browns and reds, waste material. But the tightness of the weave was skillful. The comfort with which she wore the piece suggested it had never been slept in. Then there was the matter of the draping fold which defined the neckline; a deep, inviting curve, too tasteful to have been Vigram\u8217\'92s decision. The man would probably have her naked. And if she were his slave, he wouldn\u8217\'92t be staring at her like he was about to stamp a return on interest. He wanted her, and he only ever wanted what he did not already have.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Isn\u8217\'92t she a subject fit for holy oils?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked, squeezing out a suggestive smile.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Undoubtedly,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and rare for him, he meant it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She is the Lady Pel,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93I should mention that she is interested in becoming your patroness, so be on your best behavior.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Pleased to meet you,\u8221\'94 Pel said cynically, as though she\u8217\'92d never been been pleased in her life. She held out her arm, exposing her wrist. A thin gold bracelet choked the softest flesh. Hand out, fingers down, her bejeweled ring glistened. There was a clear expectation that it should be kissed. \u8220\'93Vigram has told me everything about you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I doubt that,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. He took her hand and shook it. \u8220\'93For one thing, I don\u8217\'92t paint anymore, so if you\u8217\'92re wanting me to rough up some backwater temple icon, you\u8217\'92ll have to find someone else.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Back}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 water?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Pel scoffed. She gave Vigram a reproving look. \u8220\'93Does he always express himself so cheaply?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram shrugged. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is as I said, the boy borders on insulting.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Does he?\u8221\'94 Pel said. She lifted her chin. And without asking if Mandri minded, her green eyes flew through the details of his being: his unkempt hair, his patchy chin, his skinny neck, his flea-bag robe. When she saw his ratty shoes, she sneered. \u8220\'93He is barely even here,\u8221\'94 she said, and then she caught his eye. \u8220\'93I wonder if your insult was an attempt to distract me from seeing how boring you are.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri ___. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you not some sort of priestess?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Of a kind, yes.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, I have no interest in reviving the image your dead god. People ought to get on with their lives instead of spending what little money they have on prayers that don\u8217\'92t get answered. Sorry.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel patronized him with a grunt. It reminded him of why he didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t like serious people\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 they were too transparent. Those questing green eyes of hers, too obvious. Did she not know that she was supposed to hide her judgment behind a good ten layers of irony, so that anything she said could, in polite company, be walked back?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She took a bold step forward.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 His legs began to sweat.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 His body was readying for flight.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you a little bully?\u8221\'94 she snipped.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh,\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered. He looked to Vigram for help, but the man was busy staring at her body like it owed him something. Mandri dared not risk a peek himself, but damn, she was tall. Too tall. And too close. Her alluring lilac scent made him blush. \u8220\'93I think I\u8217\'92m a nice enough guy,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Forgive me,\u8221\'94 Vigram interjected. \u8220\'93I would have prepared the boy, but I thought\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s no need,\u8221\'94 Pel chirped. She stepped back and waved Vigram off. \u8220\'93There is no need. He is fitting the mold. You have done well to find him.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s good,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, relieved. \u8220\'93I should say that it is }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 very}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  good.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 He smiled at Mandri with a hint of pride.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93A mold for what?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked. He crossed his arms so that Pel would know that he could be serious, too. \u8220\'93What, exactly, are you looking to hire me for? I don\u8217\'92t do sculpture, or poetry either. I\u8217\'92m a farmer.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram chuckled, \u8220\'93You are not a farmer. I have seen your farm\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 it is not a farm.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Whatever he is,\u8221\'94 Pel said, \u8220\'93I will decide for myself.\u8221\'94 She turned and sort of sashayed towards the stool in which she would strike a pose. Her figure from the back was stunning. \u8220\'93For now, I will watch him work.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I\u8217\'92m only here to teach,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Vigram is the one who\u8217\'92ll be painting.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel tossed a smirk over her shoulder. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You can learn everything about a person by watching them teach. Especially if the student is difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram gasped. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am the }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 ideal}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  student! Aren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t I, Mandri? Tell her how excited you are about my progress. You were just telling me about it. Tell her!\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m very excited,\u8221\'94 Mandri said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So it is!\u8221\'94 Vigram declared. \u8220\'93Now, we should begin. But first\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 someone quiet that animal!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An old, yellow headed ox was mooing down in the nearest leech lake. It was angry at being stuck inside its stall, and also, at being bled to death. It mooed again. It bucked against its restraints. It gave a desperate, plaintive plea: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mrruuuuuu!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Get that beast\u8217\'92s snout stuck in some weed!\u8221\'94 Vigram roared. Down below, a few leechmen stumbled out of their marshgrass daydreams. They adjusted their wide-brim hats, and scurried towards the ox. \u8220\'93And you,\u8221\'94 Vigram said to Mandri, \u8220\'93help Pel onto her stool. I\u8217\'92ll ready the canvas and paint.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed a sigh for the old ox. He wished he had the courage to moo like that. He privately resolved to never eat a Meskalimi leech again. Then he did what he was told and helped Pel up onto her high-legged stool. He tried to avoid eye contact, but that didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t much help because he could feel her staring, and her presence...well, a beautiful woman\u8217\'92s presence, to a lonely man, was the worst of all oppressions. When her fingers lingered on his wrist, he began to suspect that she had some idea of power.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram eventually settled down and positioned himself in front of the canvas. When he picked up stick of soft charcoal, the lesson began.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The first exploratory marks were always difficult. Every work of art must be built on a firm foundation; get it wrong and everything that comes after will be wrong as well. Unfortunately for Vigram, he had that all too common beginner\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s habit of refusing to use his god damned brain. He started drawing wherever his hand happened to land, and whatever happened next was up to Solraheen. The end result was that Pel\u8217\'92s head was half the size it needed to be. It was also too left-of-center. There\u8217\'92d be an awkward expanse behind the healthy sweep of hair.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hold on,\u8221\'94 said Mandri. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re moving too fast. Don\u8217\'92t think of this as a portrait\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not yet. All we have right now is an oval, a rectangular canvas, and where that oval sits on that canvas. All you\u8217\'92re doing is putting an oval on a rectangle.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then do it. Think about, where\u8217\'92s the best place to put that oval? How big should it be? Remember, you have the whole canvas there.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ve told me all this before.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rubbed the marks away with his palm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He studied Pel.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped again to the canvas, then scratched another black oval exactly where the first had been.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that better?\u8221\'94 he asked with all the awareness of a potted plant. \u8220\'93You think it needs to be bigger?\u8221\'94 He drew the oval again, but only slightly larger. From then on, every other mark he made was accompanied by a look back to Mandri for reassurance. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t look at me,\u8221\'94 said Mandri, frustrated. \u8220\'93Look at her.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I need to know if the marks I make are correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92re never correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 There was a glimmer of understanding in Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eye, but just as soon as it came it faded. \u8220\'93If the mark is always wrong, then how could I ever move past it? I\u8217\'92ll be redrawing the same line over and over again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You move on when you can\u8217\'92t stand to try anymore.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That sounds miserable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, feeling understood. \u8220\'93You should be defeated by the time you\u8217\'92ve finished. I\u8217\'92ve always thought that you should never feel good about what you\u8217\'92re doing, because that means you\u8217\'92re not trying hard enough. Now, finish\u8230\'85finish the basic shapes, at least.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91finished\u8217\'92 the \u8216\'91basic shapes\u8217\'92. He looked to Mandri for final approval.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s your paint,\u8221\'94 Mandri said with a shrug. \u8220\'93But you need to understand the importance of the drawing. You\u8217\'92re always drawing. Even when painting, you are drawing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know,\u8221\'94 Vigram grumbled. \u8220\'93You talk about it all the time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram made to redraw the too-large chin, but was interrupted by a loud, mournful ox bellow.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Damn it!\u8221\'94 Vigram cried, shaking his fist.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Focus,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t get distracted. Let your men do their job.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If they were doing their job, I wouldn\u8217\'92t have heard that noise!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Please,\u8221\'94 Mandri repeated. \u8220\'93Focus.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he next looked upon his canvas, he was resolved: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m done drawing! I\u8217\'92m here to paint!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He tossed his charcoal over his shoulder and picked up his favorite brush. He mixed a bluish shade of bronze\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the color of the jaw of a Jandri man who keeps a close shave\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and then he threw down the first splotches of color in a flurry. He wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t painting so much as he was assaulting the canvas. And Sol\u8217\'92s light, that bentberry fiber weave was innocent. Expensive, too, coveted for its depth of feeling, for how it made the undertones blush. Troubled by Vigram\u8217\'92s hand, those tones were bruised and near to bleeding. It was a very confused slapping around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri had to look away.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He glanced in Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s direction.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The moment his eyes wandered down the depth of her neckline, the corner of her lip perked up. He kept looking, because why else would she wear that cut if not to catch him staring? Why would she be swimming in that lilac scent? Why bite that honeyed, aching lip? Why, if Solraheen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s last will and testament was not inciting him to stare, why did the soft shadows of the vines overhead frame her piercing eyes with the most magnificent golden light? A magical vesture indeed. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, stop flirting with my muse.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not flirting,\u8221\'94 Mandri claimed. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m checking proportions.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, and how are her proportions?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The old goat\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyebrows jumped suggestively. Pel huffed in annoyance. The yellow headed ox weighed in with an oxen roar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRRUUUUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the yellow-headed ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. But the men were too skinny. The ox bucked them both into the air, then broke its constraints and jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches. Seeing this, Mandri\u8217\'92s spirit soared. He quietly cheered.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s a five silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said firmly. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ll make a bad habit if you keep stopping in the middle of the work.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t tell me what to do, boy! On }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 my}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  farm!?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aren\u8217\'92t you rich enough already? Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram drew up in rage. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles! That animal }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 defies}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rushed to a window in the trellis and ordered his men to greater action. A squad was gathered, and they hunted as a pack. They soon had the ox surrounded in the shallows of a distant lake. The ox, legs wide like a waterbug, fended off their sharpened sticks with its stubbed horns. Mooing, bleeding, fighting for its life, it charged the smallest leechman. The little man dove into the infested waters, and again, the ox was loose.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s chest swelled with both pity and admiration. Such feeling could not be tamed. He had to do something.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What if I bought it?\u8221\'94 he asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram turned around in confusion.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri found his confidence and said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll buy the ox off you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So that we can continue with the lesson. I\u8217\'92d like to get home before dark.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nonsense. We\u8217\'92ll come to it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m serious. I\u8217\'92ll buy it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That decrepit thing? Are you making fun of me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What? No.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 judging}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This isn\u8217\'92t about you, Vigram. I respect the creature. It\u8217\'92s got fight.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram said with a rueful sigh, \u8220\'93an ox won\u8217\'92t fix your barren farm, least of all }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 that}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  ox. Besides, you lead a meager existence as it is. It would halve your wage.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be fine.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re serious?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shrugged.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stroked his beard. He glared at Mandri through a puckered brow, no doubt weighing the prospect of easy money against his intense desire to dominate all life, yellow-headed ox included.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He pulled his coinpurse from out of his robe and undid the drawstring. He pulled out a full silver string, untied a quarter of it, then cupped half of that quarter in his meaty hand. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Here,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93Your pay, minus the purchase of the ox.\u8221\'94 He handed it over. \u8220\'93As for the ox, I will have to rip the leeches off before delivering it into your care. Now, please excuse me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stomped back towards the canvas and tossed his brush onto the palette, not caring that it rolled into a swatch of blue.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Wait, hold on,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93The whole point of this was to\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This matter may take a goodly while. Our lesson is over. You may leave whenever you wish.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 With that, Vigram marched down to the leech lakes to harry his servants. Two leechmen had been napping under a tree all this time, and they bore the brunt of a good scream. Vigram screamed until his bald head rumpled and turned red. But his screaming worked against him, for it stirred a few leeched cows and goats out of their drug induced reverie. Their horrid shrieks woke up others, who shrieked in turn, and now a cascade of doleful whinnies, bleats, snorts, and muleish hee-haws pricked the ear. Raised into an anger which rivaled godly thunder, Vigram yelled right back at them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I can see myself liking you,\u8221\'94 Pel said. Her statement was almost lost amidst the cacophony of animal screams.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh,\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered as he matched her gaze. \u8220\'93What?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You care for that animal\u8217\'92s suffering. I do, too.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then why didn\u8217\'92t you buy it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel slid off her stool. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because I can see the bigger picture.\u8221\'94 She wandered over to the easel. She gave Vigram\u8217\'92s painting the chuckle it deserved, then studied the paint on the palette as if those mindless swirls were a truer work of art.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She was right about the bigger picture\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 there were at least two hundred more animals still stuck in the water. Saving that single ox was not the most efficient use of resources. Then again, the whole concept of efficiency was incoherent when applied to this particular problem, because suffering in this world had no end. As the Solitants say, and as Mandri believed, Life itself was suffering. Living things must eat, and so they must kill, and killing always inflicts a pain. This godforsaken world was one big game of murder. Even the plants were co-conspirators, feeding as the did on manure. Perhaps they did more than that\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 some Old Jandri believed that immortality would be theirs if not for plants. Plants poison the air, causing old age, and then death. How did they learn t his? The dead are buried in the dirt, and who eats the dirt? Plants. Grasses, trees, lilies in the water; these were the true masters of the world. They were the reason some Old Jandri tribes braved life in the Empty Portion, because there weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t as many plants out in the Sand. Fewer flowers. One big sniff of a flower could shave weeks off one\u8217\'92s life.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri supposed he would die soon, because Pel was absolutely drenched in that lilac scent. Did she know that she was killing him?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She picked up Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s dirty brush. She twirled its horse-hair head through the muddy colors of the palette. There was enough untouched pigment for at least four more of these awkward lessons. Very expensive. She then ran the brush through an untouched slug of yellow, ignorant of the waste. Mandri tskd his tongue, picked up a wooden shim, and politely elbowed her out of the way. He then moved to scrape that precious yellow back into its little clay jar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel chuckled as she stepped aside. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You are }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 exactly}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  as Vigram described.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri scrunched up his face. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram doesn\u8217\'92t know shit about anything.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s smile settled into a smirk. \u8220\'93You are not wrong,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93And yet, he does know a confused young man when he sees one. He said that you hold yourself in such low esteem that you neglect your basic needs.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yeah, well, like I said, Vigram doesn\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You purchased a dying ox which you cannot afford. Why?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I just want some peace and quiet, that\u8217\'92s all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93As do I,\u8221\'94 Pel said, intrigued. \u8220\'93As do I\u8230\'85\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Silence lingered between them, filled with her stare.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I believe you are fit for the job,\u8221\'94 she finally said. \u8220\'93First, you must take a test. If you perform well, you will never have to worry about money again, I assure you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What\u8217\'92s the test?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Return here tomorrow morning, and you will see.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I have plans tomorrow.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, you don\u8217\'92t.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri quirked his brow. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, I do.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel closed the distance. She took his arm and stroked the back of his hand with a playful, rolling fingertip-tap. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Tomorrow morning,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93You do not want to upset me, do you?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Her green eyes laid him bare. Hers were a lover\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyes, or a murderer\u8217\'92s. It was difficult to say because there was a fine line between the two, and}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never been in this situation.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know what to do.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He trusted his legs; they were sweating fiercely.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh, sure,\u8221\'94 he said as he pulled out of her grip. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be here. Tomorrow. Right now, I\u8217\'92ve got to get going.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m late.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93For what?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, you know, attending to my wanderings.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What about your ox?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll pick it up tomorrow. See you!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He gave a parting nod, then rushed down the veranda\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s steps.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He hurried down Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lane, which was the most terrifying lane because it was sandwiched between two leech lakes. He stayed to the right because the lake on the left held leeches bigger than his arm. Instead of stalls penning in live animals, the banks of that lake were lined with bones. The lake\u8217\'92s center was a constant swirl as hundreds of those monsters swarmed just under the water\u8217\'92s surface, bunch-crawling like caterpillars, slithering like eels, desperate to get in a taste of whatever corpse had bothered to drop in. And the moment Mandri grimaced, a round, crab-trap buoy popped out of that writhing mass. It rotated around, revealing itself to be a severed head, a human head, fresh, with close cropped hair, and an upturned nose. Its open mouth was filled with leeches. A leech the size of a leg latched onto its cheek, and pulled it under.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nope!\u8221\'94 Mandri said to himself. \u8220\'93Nope, nope, nope,\u8221\'94 he repeated as he darted towards Vigram\u8217\'92s gate. Once onto the road, he quickened his pace. He didn\u8217\'92t feel out of reach until he crested the big hill that overlooked Vigram\u8217\'92s estate. Only then did he risk a look back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram and his squad of leechmen were chasing the ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s pink rump as it bounded through the marshgrass. The ox, leeches and all, dove into a hedge. Vigram roared, because he could not follow. Meanwhile, Pel stood on the veranda\u8217\'92s steps. She stared straight through the distance, right at Mandri. Her green eyes were as vivid as they\u8217\'92d been up close.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri pretended not to notice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He walked all the way to Geem\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s and used his meager pay to buy half a bushel of burgeons. They were down-valley burgeons, decent stuff, but the waxy capsule leaves were liable to split. The insides would dry out before he could get to them in the ways that he wanted to. But, that was all Geem had, so he bought them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He continued along the road, stomping his way through the muddy wheel-ruts, slapping away the flies, humming nursery rhymes, trying anything to distract himself from overthinking the sight of that severed head. Because it was only a severed head. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s all it was! It might have never belonged to a body, or been a person. There\u8217\'92s no way of knowing, really. Anything was possible. Besides, a rich man like Vigram was sure to accumulate enemies alongside the rest of his possessions. What was one little head? People were dying all the time. This world was built on murder.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about his barren farm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about relaxing under his tree.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about sipping a milky hooch spiked through with burgeon juice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He would like to escape into that hooch. It would be bliss.}}